## 3. BIOTECH & PHARMA DEEP DIVE

### 3.1 Clinical Trial Evaluation

**Prioritized endpoints (in order):**
1. Overall Survival (OS)
2. Progression-Free Survival (PFS)
3. Hazard Ratios

**Default assumption:** ALL experimental drugs do NOT work unless proven otherwise by dramatic, undeniable evidence.

**Red flags in trial design:**

| Red Flag | What to Look For |
|----------|------------------|
| **Imbalanced baselines** | Control group intentionally seeded with sicker patients |
| **Confounded combinations** | Multiple standard-of-care drugs stacked against a bare control — masks the specific drug's lack of efficacy |
| **Misestimated control groups** | Artificially extending trial timelines by miscalculating control group survival to make the drug look better |
| **Sample size manipulation** | Post-hoc analyses on tiny pools (8 mice, 37 patients) to claim significance |
| **No placebo** | Trials lacking any proper baseline control |
| **Downplayed fatalities** | Management brushing off patient deaths as anomalies |

### 3.2 Intellectual Property Analysis

**Patent hierarchy by value:**
| Patent Type | Value | Vulnerability |
|-------------|-------|---------------|
| **Composition of matter** | Highest — protects the molecule itself | Hardest to circumvent |
| **Formulation** | Medium | Can be designed around |
| **Method of use** | Low — functionally useless | Easily circumvented by generics |
| **Polymorph** | Lowest | Minimal protection |

**Patent cliff assessment workflow:**
1. Go to FDA Orange Book
2. Find earliest patent numbers
3. Check for Paragraph IV certifications (generic challenges)
4. Calculate exact year of generic cliff
5. Model revenue decline accordingly

