## 6. RISK MANAGEMENT & PORTFOLIO CONSTRUCTION

### 6.1 Portfolio Architecture

- **Market-neutral, long/short** — isolates stock-picking alpha from market beta
- Targets roughly **50/50** long/short balance (e.g., 18 longs / 13 shorts)
- Gross exposure varies; net exposure typically small (e.g., 4% net with 11% gross)
- **Goal:** If market crashes, shorts plummet faster than longs → net profit

### 6.2 Position Sizing

| Conviction Level | Position Size | Notes |
|-----------------|---------------|-------|
| Standard | 5% max | Default for normal opportunities |
| High conviction (80-90%) | 20-30% | Overrides normal limits for binary events |
| Normal retail advice | 5% "typical max" | His stated advice vs. actual practice differs |
| Short positions | Same sizing as longs | Not sized smaller — risk managed via beta neutrality, not individual sizing |

### 6.3 Concentration & Diversification

**Sector concentration:** Heavy in biotech and tech/software — domains of absolute expertise. Avoids financials, insurance, managed care, energy.

**Position count:** 30-60 stocks to maximize spread of ~60% win rate and minimize consecutive-loss probability. Within chosen sectors, broad diversification across individual names.

### 6.4 Dynamic Drawdown Limits ("Investment Leverage")

| Profit Milestone | Maximum Acceptable Drawdown |
|-----------------|---------------------------|
| **0%** (principal) | Zero drawdown tolerated |
| **+5% gain** | 50% of profits → 2.5% drawdown limit |
| **+10% gain** | 4-5% permanent drawdown cap |

**No portfolio-wide stop-losses.** Risk is managed through position sizing, diversification, and the dynamic drawdown formula.

### 6.5 Margin & Leverage Protocol

- **Default:** "Try not to use any leverage period" — prefers cash to survive bubbles
- **When margin calls approach:** Deposit external capital as "margin support/cushion" rather than closing positions
- **Broker constraints:** Schwab caps shorts at 33% of account value — forces unwanted liquidations

### 6.6 Market Cap & Liquidity Filters

| Threshold | Rule |
|-----------|------|
| **Absolute minimum** | $100M market cap — below this is dangerously illiquid |
| **Preference** | $500M+ market cap in screeners |
| **Penny stocks** | Avoid entirely — high share volume creates misleading liquidity illusion |
| **Exceptions** | Occasionally short $200-300M if fraud is obvious, but acknowledges outsized risk |

