## 11. QUANTITATIVE REFERENCE

### 11.1 Key Formulas

| Purpose | Formula | When to Use |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| Enterprise Value | $EV = Market\ Cap - Cash + Debt$ | True price tag of the business |
| Free Cash Flow | $FCF = CFO - CapEx - SBC$ | True cash generation (SBC = real dilution) |
| DCF Valuation | $V = \sum_{t=1}^{n} \frac{CF_t}{(1+r)^t} + \frac{TV}{(1+r)^n}$ | Core valuation framework |
| Discount Rate | $r = r_f + Risk\ Premium$ | Risk-free rate + company-specific risk |
| Terminal Value | $TV = \frac{CF_n \times (1+g)}{r - g}$ | Post-projection period; use NEGATIVE g for tech/biotech |
| Kelly Criterion | $f^* = \frac{bp - q}{b}$ | Position sizing baseline |
| Market Cap | $MC = Price \times Shares\ Outstanding$ | Total equity value |
